        "date": "2026-10-15T09:41:10Z"
      },
      "message": "Smooth laneless curvature more in slow traffic\n\nIn the laneless path controlsd smooths modelV2.action.desiredCurvature with a fixed\n0.1 s time constant (LatSmoothSec only applies to the lane-line path), and the ISO\ncurvature-rate limit is loose at low speed. In 7-25 km/h traffic this passes short\n0.5-2 Hz left-right model jitter straight to the wheel (about 3.5 deg peak-to-peak;\nthe desired curvature explains ~91 % of the output swing).\n\nUse 0.3 s up to 25 km/h, ramping back to 0.1 s at 35 km/h.\nA 100 Hz rlog replay of two C4 drives (tau=0.1 reproduces the logged\ndesiredCurvature, correlation 1.0) gives 25 % lower high-passed curvature in the\n7-25 km/h band, about 0.2 s extra delay and 93-95 % peak curvature on deliberate\nlow-speed turns.\n\nAn earlier version kept 0.1 s below 4 km/h (ramping up to 7 km/h) for tight\nmanoeuvres. Drives with it showed straight-road command-angle jitter of 1.3-2.3 deg\n(high-passed RMS) below 4 km/h against 0.4 deg in the smoothed band, while the extra\n0.2 s there is under 0.2 m of travel at 3 km/h, so the low-speed exception is dropped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nDocs-Not-Needed: 일반 레인리스 경로의 내부 평활화 계수만 변경하며, 설정 항목과 기존 설정의 의미·적용 경로는 변경하지 않습니다.",
